Package: SilvaR
Title: Tools for Managing and Analyzing Data from Polish Forests
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Paweł", "Hawryło", email = "pawel.hawrylo@urk.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Piotr", "Janiec", email = "piotr.janiec@urk.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cph")),
    person("Michał", "Woda", email = "michal.woda@krakow.buligl.pl", role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Tools for processing, cleaning, and analysing forest data commonly 
    used in Polish forestry. The package provides functions for standardizing 
    species names, preparing tree and stand attributes, and calculating 
    height and volume based on widely applied empirical models, including 
    Bruchwald equations. It also includes methods for estimating top height 
    from airborne laser scanning (ALS) canopy height models (CHM) and for 
    modelling tree and stand growth over time. The tools are designed to support 
    foresters, forest managers, ecologists, and environmental scientists working 
    with tree-, plot-, and stand-level data. Development of the package is 
    carried out at the Faculty of Forestry, University of Agriculture in Krakow, 
    in collaboration with the Forest Management and Forest Geodesy Bureau (BULiGL), 
    Krakow Regional Office.
